    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes. ＜Piercing＞ has already activated. Perform the additional check, assuming your Digimon still has ＜Security A. +1＞.",
        "question": "I have a Digimon that gained ＜Security A. +1＞ from another card’s effect, and which also gained ＜Piercing＞ from this card’s inherited effect. I attack an opponent's Digimon with it, and perform a security check with ＜Piercing＞. The first card checked has a ＜De-Digivolve  1＞ nocategory of your opponent's Digimon. (Trash the top card. You can't trash past level 3 cards.) [Security] effect, which trashes the top card of my attacking Digimon, turning it into a Digimon without [Machine] or [Dragonkin].   This causes the Digimon to also lose ＜Piercing＞. Do I still perform the second check?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does.   [When Attacking] effects activate before your opponent gets to activate ＜Blocker＞.",
        "question": "I attack my opponent with this Digimon. If they block it with one of their Digimon, does this card's effect activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
